# Family A28: retry lane placement (internal/engine). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/engine
BENCH=BenchmarkMemory/OrderedRetry
REF=blocklane
AUTO_KEY=retry
KIND_DIM=""
KINDS_TEST=TestRetryKindsList
AUTO_FILE=./internal/engine/auto_retry.go
AUTO_PREFIX=RetryLane
ADR=14
TITLE="Retry lane placement (A28)"
# The engine hosts three families, so the retry placement has its own list
# test and its own generated binding:
#   hack/bakeoff.sh A28
# and `bakeoff decide` writes the binding with -auto-prefix RetryLane into
# internal/engine/auto_retry.go. The kind is the first path segment of the
# benchmark name rather than a key=value dimension, which is why KIND_DIM is
# empty. The §9 criterion is throughput at ordering=relaxed with
# failrate=10 — the arm a real workload sits in — and the ordering=strict
# arms are reported alongside it, since every kind blocks its lane there and
# the difference is what blocking costs.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="correctness for strict ordering, then latency"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: this root has no IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX branch
# and its six rows per kind cross §9.1's strict and relaxed ordering with the
# failure rates the retry lane exists for.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="ordering=strict ordering=relaxed failrate=0 failrate=10 failrate=50"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op msgs/s retries/op"
